        "body": "## Why\n\nPR D of spec 010 (`specs/010-dashboard-read-api/tasks.md`, Phase 5, US3). The dashboard can now show how the fabric's drift and the loop's activity changed over time, from the audit trail alone, over any range. A period with no scans shows as a gap, not as zero.\n\nCloses #163\nRefs #101\n\n## What Changed\n\n- **`project_series` (T036)**, `dashboard/projections.py`, research R8:\n  - **`drifted_devices`** and **`undesired_paths`**: one point per completed `ScanDrift`, at its end, so a drift spike isn't averaged away. `drifted_devices` is the scan's own `drifted` count. `undesired_paths` sums that scan's per-device `undesired_paths`. A scan with a pre-FR-012a record gets `null` (unknown), not a guess.\n  - **`deploys`** and **`repairs`**: counted per bucket by `succeeded` and `failed`. Buckets are UTC-aligned (`5m`, `1h`, `1d`, and `1w` starting Monday). A bucket where no scan, deploy or counted repair happened returns `null` for both outcomes, not 0.\n  - **Markers**: one per `ReconcileDevices` run and one per `DriftResponse` run in `remediate` mode, each with its trigger. They reuse PR C's run splitting and trigger rules.\n  - **`first_event_at`**: the oldest audit event. More than 2,000 buckets raises `ValueError`.\n- **`GET /api/v1/history` (T037)**:\n  - `series` is repeatable and defaults to all four.\n  - `start` and `end` must carry an offset; a naive time gets `422`. They default to the last 24 h.\n  - `bucket` defaults to `1h`.\n  - `start >= end`, more than 2,000 buckets, or an unknown series or bucket gets `422`.\n  - The range is never clamped to the data.\n- **The page (T038)**: a \"Last 24 hours\" table, one row per hour, refreshed every 60 s. Each row shows scans, the most drifted devices, the most undesired paths, deploys and repairs. An idle hour shows \"no scans\". Markers are listed below the table.\n- **Performance test (T034)**: `test_dashboard_performance.py`, marked `slow`. On 100,000 events, `project_devices`, `project_runs` and a 30-day `1h` series must each take under 1 s (SC-007).\n\n## How to Review\n\n- **Judgement calls**:\n  - **Failed and cancelled scans** produce no point in the per-scan series. They still mark their bucket as active for the counted series, so that bucket shows zeros rather than `null`.\n  - **Cancelled deploys** count as neither `succeeded` nor `failed`, but they make their bucket active.\n  - **Repairs** count only `succeeded` and `failed`. `unknown` and `skipped` are left out, as in R7.\n  - **Weeks start on Monday 00:00 UTC.** That is my reading of \"UTC-aligned\".\n  - **Every series carries the same markers.** The model gives each series a `markers` list, and the marked runs don't depend on the series.\n- **Follows the spec literally, flagged for spec 011**: the 2,000-bucket cap also applies to the per-scan series, even though they ignore `bucket`. So six months of `drifted_devices` at the default `1h` gets `422` unless the caller passes `1d` or `1w`.\n- **Contract gap**: `/history` returns `series` with no `View`, as the contract specifies. An unreadable audit trail therefore looks like an empty history on this route. `/devices` already reports the failure, and `/api/v1/sources` (PR F) will too.\n- **Known limitation, as in PR C**: history isn't scoped to the use case. A `test_edge` scan in the same audit trail would add to `drifted_devices`.\n- **Performance**: on 100,000 events, `project_devices` and `project_runs` take about 0.02 s each. Each series takes about 0.15 s with coverage tracing on, which is how CI runs this test, and about 0.05 s without. T036's fallback (incremental indexes in `AuditSource`) isn't needed.\n- **OpenAPI snapshot**: the change is additive. I checked every existing path and schema against the previous snapshot and none changed.\n- **Size**: about 1,010 lines, over the 400-line guide. Of that, the snapshot is 317, tests 410 (142 of them the performance test), the page 73, and the code about 200.\n\n## Live check\n\nThis is not live evidence. I ran the real server against a copy of `audit_demo_arc.sqlite`, with Temporal and the SoT on dead ports, over the capture's hour at `5m` buckets:\n\n```text\nhistory 200 0.003s\ndrifted_devices  21:20:13 \u2192 2, 21:20:15 \u2192 2, 21:20:18 \u2192 1     (the three scans in the capture)\nundesired_paths  1, 1, 1                                         (leaf-01's ethernet-1/7 description)\ndeploys          21:15 \u2192 6 succeeded, 21:20 \u2192 2 succeeded        (six operator deploys, then the reconcile's two)\nmarkers          reconcile (operator)\nnaive start      422\n```\n\n## Deferred to the lab\n\nNone in this slice.\n\n## How to Test\n\n```bash\nuv run pytest tests/unit -q                      # 995 passed\nuv run invoke lint && uv run mypy packages/ && uv run bandit -r packages/ -c pyproject.toml -q\n```\n\n## Impact & Rollout\n\n- [x] Backward compatible: a new route and new schemas only\n- [x] No new dependencies\n- [x] No config changes required\n\n## TDD Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests written before implementation (TDD). The series and route tests were run and seen to fail first, on the missing `project_series` and the missing route.\n- [x] All new source files have corresponding test files (no new source files)\n- [ ] Failing test demonstrated before fix (bug fixes only): n/a\n- [x] Coverage threshold met on new code: `projections.py` 99%, `app.py` 99%\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests added/updated\n- [x] Linting passes (`uv run invoke lint`, plus mypy and bandit)\n- [x] Changelog fragment added: `changelog/101.added.md` (appended)\n- [x] Documentation updated: tasks.md ticked (T033 to T038)\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
